  "summary_en": "This is the French Presidency's promotional dossier for the AI Action Summit (10–11 February 2025). It presents France's national AI strategy since 2018 and more than €2.5bn of investment in research and technology. It also covers AI talent and training programmes, public computing infrastructure, and low-carbon electricity. It promotes 35 sites for AI data centres and streamlined procedures. The focus is attracting investment, not regulation.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "National AI Strategy phases: €1.5bn for research (2018-2022), €1bn via France 2030, and phase 3 focused on deployment",
   "Goal of training 100,000 students and professionals in AI each year through 9 AI Clusters",
   "35 sites identified for AI data centres, some able to host projects of up to 1GW",
   "Creation of INESIA, a national institute for AI evaluation and security, and the 'AI Cafés' public debate initiative",
   "Low-carbon nuclear electricity and tax rebates offered to attract data centres"
